    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 58 tests pass and the build succeeds. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI changed owner deletion from a hard delete to a soft-delete. Changes made:\n\n**Domain / persistence**\n- `model/Owner.java` \u2014 added a `deleted` boolean column (defaulting to `false`) with getter/setter.\n- `db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql` \u2014 added `deleted BOOLEAN DEFAULT FALSE NOT NULL` to the `owners` table so existing seed rows and inserts get `false`.\n\n**API contract**\n- `resources/openapi.yml` \u2014 added a read-only `deleted` boolean to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct maps it automatically.\n\n**Behavior**\n- `service/ClinicServiceImpl.deleteOwner` \u2014 now sets `deleted = true` and `save`s the owner instead of removing the row. The controller's `DELETE` still returns `204 No Content` (2xx) and `findOwnerById` still returns the (now-flagged) record, so `GET` afterward returns `200` with `deleted: true`.\n- `rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1` \u2014 added an `isNotDeleted` helper and applied it to the create endpoint's blocking checks: `rejectDuplicateIdentity`, `rejectDuplicateHousehold`, and `findPossibleDuplicateOf`. A soft-deleted owner is now ignored, so a normally-blocking duplicate is allowed when the only matching owner has been deleted.\n\nVerification: the new `Cp46Tests` (soft-delete flags & retains; deleted owner ignored by duplicate check) pass, and the full suite is green \u2014 **58 tests, 0 failures, BUILD SUCCESS**.",
